\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.2}{\ignorespaces Cost-vector for self-consistent diffusion estimation in confinement. Here, a $\sim \SI {100}{\nm }$ Polystyrene bead was imaged and tracked in the transverse plane. The initial size estimate before confinement analysis was $\hat  {a} = \SI {124.30}{\nm }$. Post self-consistency, applying a linear superposition theory estimate of the confinement effects, $a^* = \SI {64.1}{\nm }$.}}{12}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:diff_self_cons}{{2.2}{12}{Cost-vector for self-consistent diffusion estimation in confinement. Here, a $\sim \SI {100}{\nm }$ Polystyrene bead was imaged and tracked in the transverse plane. The initial size estimate before confinement analysis was $\hat {a} = \SI {124.30}{\nm }$. Post self-consistency, applying a linear superposition theory estimate of the confinement effects, $a^* = \SI {64.1}{\nm }$}{figure.caption.12}{}}
