\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {5.1}Optical System Diagram}{31}{section.5.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Isometric iSCAT Schematic. A laser is first shaped using a spatial filter for a gaussian beam profile. The gaussian beam is sized by an aperture and focused into the back-plane of an objective. During the focusing, the light is circularily polarized. At the sample plane, two coverslips are placed for sample containment. To control the gap between the two coverslips, the convex-lens induced confinement (CLiC) system is used. The scattered and reflected light is collected through a polarizing beam-splitter and the final image is focused on a CMOS camera array.}}{32}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:schematic}{{5.1}{32}{Isometric iSCAT Schematic. A laser is first shaped using a spatial filter for a gaussian beam profile. The gaussian beam is sized by an aperture and focused into the back-plane of an objective. During the focusing, the light is circularily polarized. At the sample plane, two coverslips are placed for sample containment. To control the gap between the two coverslips, the convex-lens induced confinement (CLiC) system is used. The scattered and reflected light is collected through a polarizing beam-splitter and the final image is focused on a CMOS camera array}{figure.caption.19}{}}
